<mxGraphModel><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;whiteSpace=wrap;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;LaminarFlow-Frontend/src/api/client.ts&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="30" width="760" y="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="3" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Andale Mono&quot;&gt;module&lt;/font&gt; — no function is declared; the file exports one const, &lt;font face=&quot;Andale Mono&quot;&gt;api&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;api is a typed openapi-fetch client over the generated paths type from&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;src/api/schema.d.ts, which is generated from the backend&#39;s OpenAPI document&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;and is not carded here — reached from every feature&#39;s api/ folder, and nothing&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;else in the app ever constructs a client of its own&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="100" width="760" y="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="4" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Imports&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;import createClient from &#39;openapi-fetch&#39;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;import type { paths } from &#39;./schema&#39;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;export const &lt;b&gt;api&lt;/b&gt; = createClient&amp;lt;paths&amp;gt;({ … })&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="100" width="760" y="390" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="5" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Returns nothing to a caller — the module-level const api is itself the export: a&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Client&amp;lt;paths&amp;gt; singleton whose .GET / .POST / … are constrained by the generated&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;paths, so a URL the backend does not serve, or a response field it does not send,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;is a TypeScript error rather than a runtime surprise.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="80" width="760" y="490" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="6" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;-&amp;gt; api: Client&amp;lt;paths&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="30" width="760" y="570" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="7" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;{&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;baseUrl: location.origin,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;fetch: (request) =&amp;gt; globalThis.fetch(request),&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;baseUrl is the page&#39;s own origin, so every call stays same-origin and relative: in&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;production the Go binary serves this bundle and the API from one port, and in dev&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Vite proxies /api and /healthz across to :8080, so no host is ever hard-coded&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;the fetch wrapper looks globalThis.fetch up at call time instead of capturing it&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;once, which is what lets a test swap the global out from under this client&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="220" width="760" y="600" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel>
